===Etymology 2===
{{etymid|fi|look}}
A dialectal or colloquial 2nd person imperative present of {{m|fi|katsoa||to look}}. The corresponding infinitive is {{m|fi|kattoa}}.

====Pronunciation====
{{fi-pronunciation|*}}

====Verb====
{{head|fi|verb form}}

# {{lb|fi|colloquial}} [[look]]!
#: '''''Kato''', tuolla on George!'' &mdash; ''Look, there's George!''
# {{lb|fi|colloquial}} [[see]] (used often with [[nyt|ny]])
#: '''''Kato''' ny, mähän sanoin.'' &mdash; ''See, I told you so.''

=====Synonyms=====
* {{l|fi|katso}}
* {{l|fi|ka}} {{qual|colloquial}}

====Interjection====
{{fi-int}}

# {{lb|fi|colloquial}} [[see]] or [[look]].
#: ''Se on '''kato''' sillä lailla.''
#:: '''''See''', that’s the way it is.''
#: '''''Kato''' nääs!'' or '''''Kato kato!'''''
#:: Literally: ''Look, look!.'' Uttered in surprise, not necessarily telling anyone to look anywhere.
#: '''''Kato nääs''', säkin olet saapunut paikalle.''
#:: '''''Lo and behold''', you have arrived on the scene, too.''
#: ''...'''kato''' nääs.'' or ''...'''kato.'''''
#:: ''...you see.'' (At the end of a sentence)

